A||||5||JohnnyK||What could happen on the way to CT?||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||08-23-2000||04:40 PM||||Ok, I'm thinking about taking the not so reliable Fiero, or the reliable Accord. What could go wrong on a 10 hr trip? What are some things that usually go wrong with Fieros.||||reg||1
Z||000001||whamel||08-23-2000||04:53 PM||||Geez, I'd take the accord if there was any doubt!  I once took my '81 Z-28 for a spin from Cincinnati to Cleveland and totally smoked the car the day after I finished restoring it.  (big cloud of smoke, big bang - car no go!  I believe the flywheel broke, but I never figured it out.)  I ended up having to sell the car in Cleveland, take a huge loss on it, plus having to try and figure out how the heck I'm going to get home (greyhound bus..how embarrassing!).  <BR>I'd have to say it would sure be fun to take a trip in a Fiero, but I remember taking mine from LA to Las Vegas when I picked it up from the dock and it was a nightmare.  The thing was overheating in traffic, plus it had some other issues from it's boat ride, by the time I got to Vegas I was so burned out from worrying about making it that it wasn't worth the effort.  (My car had just left Anchorage, AK and was really set up for deep cold, not extreme heat!)The only thing I could think about was that if this thing broke down so far from home, I'd be out my favorite car and there was little I could have done about it at the time.  I got lucky! ||||reg||1
Z||000002||RiceCooker||08-23-2000||07:11 PM||||Not trying to cut whamel down, but a fiero is NOT a camaro. My fiero has been on a lot of 8 hour drives through the mountains and has been great on the highway all the time.<P>I drove across the country this spring on a 14hour trip each way. I know that my fiero runs very cool on the highway and you don't even have to shift so if you do have a problem, it's just $hitty luck. <P>If you take good care of your car, and it runs fine in the city, enjoy your trip.<P>For my long trips, i carry an extra quart of oil, first aid kit, emergency tools, extra water, and even a small fire extinguisher all up in the front compartment. You can't go wrong with that.||||reg||14
Z||000003||RiceCooker||08-23-2000||07:13 PM||||Oh yeah, my 86se has 185,000 km.<BR>approx 115miles||||reg||1
Z||000004||HugGRRRFiero||08-23-2000||07:40 PM||||Have you had any recent DNF's with your Fiero?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">   Do you have any unresolved check engine lights?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">  Any unexplainable noises?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  Any fluttering gauges?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">  If you have, you have already entered the Fiero Zone!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  Just kidding, if you do, I'd go with the Accord.  Do the fluids check, radiator fan check, alternator belt check etc...<P>Brent<BR><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">  <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||whamel||08-23-2000||10:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by RiceCooker:<BR><B>Not trying to cut whamel down, but a fiero is NOT a camaro. My fiero has been on a lot of 8 hour drives through the mountains and has been great on the highway all the time.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>     Okay - next time I'll call it 'Car X' just to make it fair.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  He said in his initial message that his Fiero was already 'unreliable' - I thought 'Car X' was reliable since I had just rebuilt the engine from scratch (live and learn, eh?), but I didn't do some things I should have I guess and screwed it up.  Regardless - I thought the car could do the trip and I was wrong.  I was also out about $4000 when all was said and done!  <BR>Don't get me wrong - I'm planning on driving my Fiero to Chicago in a few weeks.  I have great faith in Pontiac (heck, I've owned 18 or 19 Ponchos so far) and great faith in the Fiero.  But when a car is dubbed 'unreliable' from the start..well...<BR>Perhaps I should hear a bit more detail of the problems this particular car has before I make judgement on it, eh?<BR>Wade<P>||||reg||1
